Hardcourt bike polo is a fast-paced team sport played on an enclosed hard court.

Three players per team ride bikes and use mallets to knock a small ball into the opposing team's goal — first to five points wins.

Players who touch the ground ("dab") must tap out at center court before rejoining play.

Invented by bike messengers in the Pacific Northwest in the late 1990s, the sport has since spread to over 300 cities across 30+ countries.
